                    {
                        "sense_id": "7a082d68-6781-3645-bdb6-ef7dd73d0876",
                        "entry_id": "b60dd041-fa92-38cf-bb47-f8dbb5d4ba7c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "État minimal dont la légitimité est enserrée par des limites strictes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c27423c3-e12f-475d-8ba3-75ea3b8c44f9",
                                "sense_id": "7a082d68-6781-3645-bdb6-ef7dd73d0876",
                                "text": "Pour Noczik, la gestion privée de la sécurité ne pourrait déboucher que sur le monopole d’une agence, qui conduirait de facto à la création d’un État minimal, dont les pouvoirs respecteraient et garantiraient les droits des individus : la « minarchie »."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "076a4c77-e7c4-44ef-a215-75a38dce8aad",
                        "source_entry_id": "b60dd041-fa92-38cf-bb47-f8dbb5d4ba7c",
                        "source_sense_id": "7a082d68-6781-3645-bdb6-ef7dd73d0876",
                        "target_lang_word": "minarchy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "minarchy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b953dfa0-bea0-3c2f-bcd9-6dd15379fb5c",
                                        "entry_id": "7641675e-6ca3-3466-abbf-75afb850e96d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Government with the least necessary power over its citizens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7e763a0-a7b2-4a98-872c-38e069a66873",
                                                "sense_id": "b953dfa0-bea0-3c2f-bcd9-6dd15379fb5c",
                                                "text": "This \"minarchy,\" often dubbed the \"nightwatchman State,\" reduced to police (and possibly army), is their historical ideal - and even in present days that of philosopher Nozick, for instance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83abbedf-d9cf-4373-a7b7-f04e22bfe4e3",
                                                "sense_id": "b953dfa0-bea0-3c2f-bcd9-6dd15379fb5c",
                                                "text": "In minarchy the owner of a property is the sole owner of the private propety and what comes out of it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4811e2fa-f0ff-48e1-8bb7-78068cfea6cf",
                                                "sense_id": "b953dfa0-bea0-3c2f-bcd9-6dd15379fb5c",
                                                "text": "But even the most minimal minarchy, at some point, must claim its citizens' exclusive allegiance"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f0cbe917-36f7-432b-83bc-bc0279b2bde4",
                        "source_entry_id": "b60dd041-fa92-38cf-bb47-f8dbb5d4ba7c",
                        "source_sense_id": "7a082d68-6781-3645-bdb6-ef7dd73d0876",
                        "target_lang_word": "night watchman state",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "night watchman state",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d21d43e-32f9-36b9-95dc-8fe489c99711",
                                        "entry_id": "89def38f-1574-3850-82f0-abc68595257f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Government that is limited to a bare minimum of functions, usually just military, police, and courts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53049495-808a-4811-b8f8-4d4b67c96a9a",
                                                "sense_id": "6d21d43e-32f9-36b9-95dc-8fe489c99711",
                                                "text": "The doctrines of conservative liberalism were propounded by the late nineteenth century's leading intellectual proponents of the night watchman state."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05dc5fa0-6939-4286-83ac-4f4fd00f1c3b",
                                                "sense_id": "6d21d43e-32f9-36b9-95dc-8fe489c99711",
                                                "text": "For these neoLiberal^([sic]) Democrats of the Orange Book school remain determined to junk social liberalism for economic liberalism. Their guiding light is the Gladstonian ideal of a low tax, laissez-faire, “night-watchman state”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
